    wordCount: 550,
    text: `Science and technology play an important role in modern society by helping people understand the world, solve practical problems, improve productivity, and develop new products and services. Scientific research generates knowledge through observation, experimentation, analysis, and systematic investigation. Technology uses knowledge and skills to develop tools, processes, and systems that can address human needs. Innovation connects these activities with practical applications and can contribute to economic and social development. Research institutions, universities, laboratories, industries, and government organisations all contribute to scientific and technological progress. Basic research may focus on understanding fundamental principles, while applied research seeks solutions to specific problems. Both forms of research can be important because discoveries made through basic studies may later support useful technologies. Collaboration between academic institutions, industries, and public organisations can help move ideas from research laboratories towards practical applications. Digital technology has changed many areas of daily life. Computers, mobile devices, communication networks, and online platforms allow information to be created, processed, stored, and shared rapidly. Digital systems are used in education, banking, healthcare, transport, agriculture, public administration, and business. However, the benefits of digital technology depend on reliable infrastructure, appropriate skills, responsible use, and protection of information. Artificial intelligence is another area receiving significant attention. AI based systems can analyse large amounts of information, identify patterns, assist with predictions, and support decision making in selected applications. These systems may be useful in areas such as healthcare, agriculture, transportation, education, and administration. At the same time, their use requires careful consideration of data quality, privacy, security, transparency, and human oversight. Space technology provides another example of how scientific research can support public services. Satellites can contribute to communication, weather forecasting, navigation, disaster management, agriculture, environmental monitoring, and mapping. Scientific missions also help researchers study the Earth, the solar system, and the broader universe. The development of space technology requires specialised knowledge, engineering capabilities, testing facilities, and long term planning. Biotechnology has applications in healthcare, agriculture, environmental management, and industrial processes. Research in this field can support the development of medicines, diagnostic methods, improved crops, and other useful products. Because biotechnology can involve complex biological systems, research and applications require appropriate scientific standards, safety procedures, and ethical consideration. Renewable energy technologies are also important for reducing dependence on limited fossil fuel resources and supporting cleaner energy systems. Solar, wind, and other renewable sources can contribute to energy diversification. Research and innovation can improve efficiency, storage, transmission, and integration of renewable energy into existing systems. Innovation does not always require a completely new invention. It may involve improving an existing product, reducing production costs, developing a more efficient process, or adapting technology to local needs. Small improvements can have significant effects when they are applied widely. Education and skill development are therefore important for creating a society capable of using and developing new technologies. Scientific thinking encourages curiosity, evidence based reasoning, problem solving, and willingness to test ideas. A strong innovation ecosystem requires investment in research, skilled professionals, infrastructure, collaboration, and opportunities for experimentation. Science and technology can contribute greatly to national development when they are used responsibly and when their benefits are made accessible to different sections of society. Continued investment in research and human capabilities can help address emerging challenges and create new opportunities in the future.`
